WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.430
So this is a sample of iridium, now this is
a sponge-type

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:08.690
iridium so it is very finely divided, very,
very light weight. So,

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.520
we open the vial.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.370
Iridium is at the bottom of the group that
has cobalt and

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:20.179
rhodium, and iridium, like rhodium, can be
used in a lot of

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:21.179
catalysts.

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:25.599
And here we have the glass ampule inside and
we can see

00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:30.400
here that the iridium sample is a sponge.
Now again you can

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.380
see that this is a very, very, very light
material and you can

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.590
see it flowing inside the vial.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.989
In fact, iridium catalysts sometimes will
work much better

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:45.539
than the rhodium catalyst and there is a good
example where

00:00:45.539 --> 00:00:51.899
people have replaced rhodium with iridium
and found that

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:56.399
they can make much more compound in the same
chemical

00:00:56.399 --> 00:01:01.559
plant and this is really good because then
you get more stuff

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:05.770
coming out without having to have any more
metal work.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.729
Chemical engineers have a very nice name for
this it is called

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:12.300
de-bottlenecking when you get more for the
same amount of

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:12.639
plant.

